.TH "TDDA TAG" 1 "April 2026" "3.0" "tdda tag manual"
.SH NAME
\fBtdda tag\fR  -- tag tests that failed in the last reference test run

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtdda tag\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBtdda tag\fR command reads the log of failing tests written by the most
recent reference test run and adds \fB@tag\fR decorators to those tests in
their source files. Tagged tests can then be run in isolation, allowing
a rapid edit-test cycle focused on failing tests.

.PP
Before \fBtdda tag\fR can be used, tests must be run with failure logging
enabled, which writes the IDs of failing tests to a log file.

.SH WORKFLOW
A typical workflow with \fBunittest\fR-style tests (\fBReferenceTestCase\fR) is:

.PP
\fBpython tests.py -9      # Remove any existing @tag decorators\fR
.br
\fBpython tests.py -F      # Run tests, logging failures\fR
.br
\fBtdda tag                # Add @tag to failing tests\fR
.br
\fBpython tests.py -1      # Run only tagged (failing) tests\fR

.PP
When all tests are passing:

.PP
\fBpython tests.py -9      # Remove @tag decorators\fR

.PP
The equivalent workflow with \fBpytest\fR is:

.PP
\fBpytest --untag          # Remove any existing\fR@tag\fBdecorators\fR
.br
\fBpytest --log-failures   # Run tests, logging failures\fR
.br
\fBtdda tag                # Add @tag to failing tests\fR
.br
\fBpytest --tagged         # Run only tagged (failing) tests\fR

.PP
When all tests are passing:

.PP
\fBpytest --untag          # Remove @tag decorators\fR

.SH SEE ALSO
tdda(1),
tdda-reftest(1),
tdda-reftest-unittest(1),
tdda-reftest-pytest(1)
